  "title": "Community models became easier to build and trust",
  "summary": "This week made it easier to publish, find, and use community-built models and apps, while tightening the plumbing underneath them.\n\nBuilders gained endpoint probes, image-model support in polli CLI, and OpenAI-compatible transcription for community speech models. Text-model listings now show capabilities and access requirements; unhealthy endpoints stay callable by exact ID but leave catalogs and fallback routing until they recover. Publishing guides now cover text, image, audio, video, and agents. Managed agents gained inspectable tool-call records and can discover tools advertised by enabled MCP servers.\n\nQwen3.8 27B, GLM-5.3, and Quest-accessible Nemotron 3.5 Lightning expanded the reasoning and tool-use roster. Grok TTS and Fish Audio S2.1 Pro added speech options, while GPT transcription joined uploaded-audio and live-session APIs. Video model metadata now exposes supported durations so apps can build pickers that match each model.\n\nNew directory entries ranged from Android image generation and browser playgrounds to anime art, Roblox character chat, cursor design, and collaborative image-making. Shareable search URLs and reorganized browsing controls make the growing directory easier to explore. The model catalog also gained clearer pricing, capabilities, publisher details, and mobile layouts.\n\nImage edits without a specified size now derive an output shape from the source instead of defaulting to a square. Community image endpoints gained consistent URL and base64 handling with a bounded streamed download path, and Kontext generation and editing were pointed at a working deployment. Fewer surprises between sending a picture and getting one back.",
